# Platform Color Convention

When any output (chart, diagram, HTML, SVG, etc.) involves platform-specific data or labels, use the following brand colors consistently:

| Platform | Color | Hex |
|----------|-------|-----|
| **WLW** (Wer liefert was) | Blue | `#1f6feb` / `#58a6ff` (light variant) |
| **EP** (Europages) | Green | `#2ea043` / `#3fb950` (light variant) |
| **Alibaba** | Yellow/Orange | `#d29922` / `#e3b341` (light variant) |

## Rules

- Use the primary hex on dark backgrounds; use the light variant on white/light backgrounds.
- When both WLW and EP appear together, they must be visually distinguishable by these colors — never swap or assign arbitrary palette colors.
- Legend labels, data series, highlights, borders, and area fills should all follow this convention.
- If a chart only involves one platform, the brand color is still preferred over a generic palette.
